  "about": "The recorded pitches of the app's piano from MIDI 33 to 90, the sources of the site's web piano. Facts copied from test/fixtures/piano/manifest.json, where every field is explained: Written by tool/render_piano_samples.py. One entry per key; checked by test/piano_tuning_test.dart. Cents are against 12-TET, A4 = 440 Hz. f0Cents: the fundamental (first partial, located by partial fit), energy-weighted median of 0.3 s frames from 0.15 to 1.5 s. yinCents: the live detector's YIN over the same span, i.e. the piano's inharmonicity offset; null where it gives under 5 readings (under 43 Hz, and C8, which it stops following after 0.2 s). clipScoreCents / clipYinCents: the score reader (YIN + band refiner) and plain YIN on the clip, energy-weighted, by the Python port. loudnessDb: RMS of the first 0.5 s. gainDb: the peak level the note was set to; cutDb: how far under the loudness curve, 0 on it. Frames are 44.1 kHz; the clip is frames [clipStartFrame, +clipFrames) of the decoded file, and clipSha256 the hash of its WAV in clips/.",
